Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.

The Community You Will Join:&nbsp;

The Airbnb Communications team is responsible for telling Airbnb’s story around the world.&nbsp;

We help drive consideration and usage of our products and services in addition to generating buzz, supporting the legitimization of our community, and promoting trust in our brand. We lead the communications strategy to make Airbnb synonymous with magical travel and the world’s leading platform for hospitality entrepreneurs.&nbsp;

We speak to the media, influencers, hosts and guests, industry commentators, thought leaders and the wider community - we are the voice of Airbnb. We’re a fast growing, high-energy team with a passion for people, places and great stories. If you’d like to be part of one of the world’s greatest teams, come tell us your story.

The Difference You Will Make:

We are hiring a Senior Communications Manager for Korea. This role leads policy and corporate reputation communications in Korea. It identifies and develops the key issues and narratives that shape how Airbnb is understood by media, policymakers and the public, builds the relationships beyond the newsroom that give those narratives weight, including the host community, academia, think tanks, and industry and professional associations, and runs the ‘always on’ press office that keeps Airbnb visible and accurately represented in Korean media every day.&nbsp;

The role works closely with the Korea Communications team members and cross-functional partners to make sure Airbnb’s position on the issues that matter in Korea is clear, credible and heard. It also provides press strategy and media counsel for consumer campaigns led by the wider team, so that those moments strengthen Airbnb’s reputation as well.

We’re looking for a seasoned communications professional with strong judgment on policy and reputation issues, a strong grasp of the Korean news and regulatory landscape, the ability to turn complex topics into clear narratives, and the relationship skills to engage journalists and external stakeholders with credibility. Disciplined on the daily basics, strategic on the issues that count.&nbsp;

The role is based in Seoul and reports to the Senior Communications Lead, Korea.

A Typical Day:

• Lead policy and corporate reputation communications in Korea, shaping the team’s strategy on key issues and turning it into plans and delivery.

• Develop narratives that shape how Airbnb is understood by media, policymakers and the public, including short-term rental regulation, trust and safety, corporate reputation, thought leadership, and Airbnb’s economic and community contribution.

• Develop messaging, holding statements, Q&amp;A, and executive briefing materials on key corporate issues, and lead reactive media handling in partnership with the Public Policy team.

• Build relationships beyond the media that lend credibility to Airbnb’s narratives, including host community representatives, academics, think tanks, industry and professional associations, and local government, and drive third-party partnerships such as research, forums and speaking opportunities that put Airbnb’s issues on the public agenda.

• Lead spokesperson preparation for media interviews, public speaking and stakeholder engagements.&nbsp;

• Strategize and run the ‘always on’ press office with local agencies: daily monitoring and issue flagging, proactive data and trend pitches, inbound media handling, and a steady drumbeat of host and community stories.

